        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamplifier",
        "description": "NE5532 dual op-amp used as the low-level preamplifier stage powered from the external single 9V supply. One amplifier channel is intended to provide the main voltage-gain path whose analog output drives the LM386 input stage. Because the brief requires single-supply operation while NE5532 has only VCC_P and VCC_N pins available in the provided data, this module depends on downstream biasing and AC-coupling/passive feedback networks to establish the required single-supply operating point and target overall gain contribution without assuming any additional active rail-generation circuitry. The second op-amp channel is available for coordinated audio-support use within the same preamp domain if needed, but the provided brief only requires that the NE5532 output feed the LM386 input.",
